00:44:41.980 --> 00:44:45.437
It says, "My apologies if this
was covered at the beginning.

00:44:45.437 --> 00:44:47.927
"Can you mention a bit
more on the practice

00:44:47.927 --> 00:44:52.927
"of slavery in Banda, any sense
of how many people enslaved

00:44:53.017 --> 00:44:55.697
"and from where and
whether intergenerational

00:44:55.697 --> 00:44:59.057
"or time bound within the
lifetime of an enslaved person?"

00:45:02.070 --> 00:45:04.530
- Yeah, so I can go into it a little bit,

00:45:04.530 --> 00:45:06.380
though I don't really specialize

00:45:06.380 --> 00:45:08.720
on the history of slavery in Banda.

00:45:08.720 --> 00:45:11.380
There are others, particularly
in the Netherlands

00:45:13.422 --> 00:45:16.713
who really delve deeply into this.

00:45:17.620 --> 00:45:20.470
There is some debate, I
think among historians

00:45:20.470 --> 00:45:25.010
about whether the practice of slavery

00:45:25.010 --> 00:45:30.010
in the Eastern archipelago is
kind of a unique case in Asia

00:45:30.820 --> 00:45:35.820
where it's much more
reminiscent of slavery

00:45:36.410 --> 00:45:40.773
in the Atlantic world, or
whether it's kind of part

00:45:43.360 --> 00:45:48.360
of the much more kind of a
household slavery system,

00:45:50.560 --> 00:45:52.533
which Anthony Reed writes about.

00:45:55.770 --> 00:45:57.950
I don't really have much of a sense

00:46:00.462 --> 00:46:04.453
of which might be correct,
but after the Banda massacre

00:46:05.830 --> 00:46:08.113
in the early 17th century,

00:46:10.978 --> 00:46:14.680
the local overseers
where basically the Dutch

00:46:14.680 --> 00:46:19.680
were brought in and were in
charge of Bandanese slaves,

00:46:21.450 --> 00:46:25.770
but also other slaves who
were brought into Banda

00:46:25.770 --> 00:46:27.853
from all over the archipelago.

00:46:29.200 --> 00:46:33.190
And over time, by the
end of the 17th century,

00:46:33.190 --> 00:46:36.333
which might talk kind of touched on,

00:46:37.420 --> 00:46:42.420
the overseers are no longer
identified as European or Dutch,

00:46:44.030 --> 00:46:47.923
or even people who have like Dutch blood.

00:46:52.060 --> 00:46:55.870
They're much more seen as
Bandanese at that point

00:46:55.870 --> 00:46:59.780
because many of them had married locally.

00:47:02.090 --> 00:47:06.240
But the slaves are also
considered Bandanese

00:47:06.240 --> 00:47:09.690
and sometimes they are
identified ethnically

00:47:11.800 --> 00:47:15.210
as being from different
parts of the archipelago.

00:47:15.210 --> 00:47:17.030
I mean, it's a really fascinating case

00:47:17.030 --> 00:47:22.030
of how identification based on ethnicity

00:47:23.130 --> 00:47:25.570
and based on the name of the island

00:47:25.570 --> 00:47:28.370
kind of comes into being
in this part of the world

00:47:28.370 --> 00:47:30.590
where of course after the massacre,

00:47:30.590 --> 00:47:34.290
you have a great
reduction of local people,

00:47:34.290 --> 00:47:35.990
but by the end of the century,

00:47:35.990 --> 00:47:40.573
you have this repopulation through force.

00:47:43.301 --> 00:47:45.320
So I'm not sure if that
answers your question,

00:47:45.320 --> 00:47:49.457
but it is, I believe, I
think it is a lifetime

00:47:53.550 --> 00:47:55.940
over the course of a person's lifetime

00:47:55.940 --> 00:48:00.263
that they serve as slaves, but
I would have to check that.

